  "scope": {
    "status": "grounded",
    "grounding_mode": "contextual_synthesis",
    "text": "SSE, also known as scatter, is used as an objective function to measure the quality of a clustering; a smaller squared error indicates that the prototypes (centroids) are a better representation of the points in their cluster. In K-means clustering, the mean is the centroid that minimizes the SSE of the cluster, and initialization methods like K-means++ aim to produce results with lower SSE.",
